# core.autocrlf is on here, so everything is stored as LF and checked out as
# CRLF. The test goldens are the exception: they hold what metadata() and
# describe_setup() return, which is joined with \n, and the tests compare them
# byte for byte. Left to the usual rule they would come back CRLF on a fresh
# clone and every output test would fail on a machine that had never seen them.
tests/golden/*.txt -text
